   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Leo. You're verified, and I've looked into order Q-7201 from Burger Barn.\n\n**What happened:**\n- The order was due by 7:00 PM. The courier picked it up at 6:40 PM.\n- The app marked it delivered at 6:58 PM, but the courier's own log shows that was 2.1 miles from your address. The order was not handed to you then.\n- The actual handoff happened at 7:47 PM, 47 minutes after the promised time.\n\n**What I did:**\n- I added a **$5.60 account credit** to your Forkful account. That is 20% of the $28.00 food subtotal, which is our compensation for a delivery that arrives 45 or more minutes late.\n\nLate deliveries are compensated with account credit rather than a refund to your card, so the credit will be available for your next order. Your current balance is $5.60.\n\nI'm sorry the app showed the order as delivered when it wasn't, and that the food reached you so late."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Right, so the app said delivered around 7 and I was sitting at home with nothing on the step until 7:45. A $5.60 credit for a burger that was almost an hour late doesn't feel like much, but I'm not going to argue the number with you. Thanks for looking into it properly. Please make sure the note about the false \"delivered\" status is on the account so it doesn't happen again."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks for being patient, Leo, and I'm sorry you waited at home for almost an hour.\n\nI can't add notes to your account, so I can't put a note on it about the false \"delivered\" status. What I can confirm is that the delivery record for Q-7201 already shows the 6:58 PM \"marked delivered\" entry was made 2.1 miles away, with the real handoff at 7:47 PM. That record is what I used for your credit.\n\nYour $5.60 credit is on the account and can be used on your next order. If you'd like a specialist to look at the app's false delivery status, I can pass your case to a human team, who will follow up within 24 hours. Would you like me to do that?"
  }
